The plate is a square plate, roughly 24 cm across. The rice mound covers about 12 x 10 cm at the widest, with a height of about 2.5-3 cm. That gives a volume of roughly 150-200 ml at a loose cooked-rice density of about 0.65-0.7 g/ml. That works out to about 110-140 g.

The small green flecks are herbs, about 1 g in total. The orange-yellow smears are oil or sauce residue, about 4 g.

